{
  "opening": "The marshmallow library is updating its field API to replace deprecated parameter names, which affects how default and missing values are configured. The fuhrysteve__marshmallow-jsonschema consumer relies on these fields to generate accurate JSON Schema definitions, so it must adapt to the new interface to function correctly.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "In the marshmallow project, Field, Nested, Constant, and Raw classes must accept load_default and dump_default parameters instead of the deprecated default and missing parameters. Using the old default or missing arguments should trigger a deprecation warning indicating that they will be removed in a future version."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02c",
      "text": "When used within the fuhrysteve__marshmallow-jsonschema context, schemas defining Field, Nested, Constant, or Raw instances must utilize load_default and dump_default for value configuration. The JSON Schema output generated by marshmallow-jsonschema must reflect the correct loading and dumping defaults as specified by these new parameters."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure both projects are aligned with this API shift before the next release to maintain compatibility and silence warnings."
}
